From 0fb809e96380d1007a23d790bb63132d4392754e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: utzcoz <utzcoz@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:31:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] webxr: support frame rate control with OpenXR

Implement XRSession.frameRate, supportedFrameRates and
updateTargetFrameRate with XR_FB_display_refresh_rate. Until now they
were stubs.

The device sends the supported rates and the current rate when the
session starts, and the current rate with every frame, so the page also
sees changes the runtime makes on its own. A new XRFrameRateController
interface passes the page's target rate to the runtime.
updateTargetFrameRate resolves once the runtime has the request,
without waiting for the switch, per
https://github.com/immersive-web/webxr/issues/1449.

Runtimes without the extension behave as before.

The WebXR Test API can't set up frame rates, so the web tests extend
the Chromium mock in wpt_internal.

Bug: 506004811
Co-authored-by: Neil Kronlage <neilkr@meta.com>
Change-Id: Ie8f902973efb65fa4bce922180a271172aaa085d
